"""The ComfyUI custom node API: ``from comfy_api.index import ComfyExtension, eng, io, ui, util``.

Public names: ``eng`` (the engine, below), ``io`` (declaring nodes), ``ui`` (what a node shows),
``util`` (pure helpers, and ``util.folders``: ComfyUI's folders by path), ``ComfyExtension``
(registering a pack's nodes, and its samplers, schedulers and model folders), and the value types
``Types``, ``Input`` and ``InputImpl``.

A node declares itself with ``io.ComfyNode``, sets ``ENGINE_API = True``, and reaches the
engine only through ``eng``::

    class SoftenCFG(io.ComfyNode):
        ENGINE_API = True

        @classmethod
        def define_schema(cls):
            return io.Schema(node_id="SoftenCFG", inputs=[io.Model.Input("model"),
                             io.Float.Input("amount", default=0.9)], outputs=[io.Model.Output()])

        @classmethod
        async def execute(cls, model, amount):
            def soften(args):
                return args["uncond"] + (args["cond"] - args["uncond"]) * args["cond_scale"] * amount
            return io.NodeOutput(await eng.model.set_cfg(model, soften))

Values:
    ``execute`` receives its inputs as they are: IMAGE and MASK tensors, LATENT dicts,
    CONDITIONING lists, plain values, and the engine's MODEL, CLIP and VAE objects. It returns
    the same kinds of values. Do tensor work with torch in the node; pass engine objects to
    ``eng`` calls rather than reaching into them, so the node runs the same wherever ComfyUI
    dispatches it.

Calls:
    Every ``eng`` call is async. Tensors and data go in and come back as themselves; engine
    objects come back as engine objects. Functions given to ``eng.model.set_*`` run during
    sampling, see only tensors and plain data, and can't make ``eng`` calls.

Engine extensions:
    Code that has to touch live engine objects beyond these calls ships as one file,
    ``v2/engine/<name>.py``, defining ``class EngineOps``. It is loaded with the pack, runs
    next to the engine, must be on ``ALLOWED_EXTENSIONS`` (file name and sha256), and is
    called as ``await eng.ext.<name>.<method>(...)``.

Not here:
    ``comfy``, ``nodes``, ``server`` and ``folder_paths`` imports; handles; ``ctx``. Use these
    calls, ``eng.node.run`` for ComfyUI's own nodes, or an engine extension; ``util.folders``
    for paths, and ``routes`` in ``pyproject.toml`` for HTTP endpoints.
"""
